:: day0_npc_brin [nobr]
<<npcPortrait "brin" "Brin">>
<h3>Servant Brin   Last Breakfast</h3>

<p>The knock comes at the usual time. Brin with the tray   bread, cheese, cold meat, the not-quite-tea. He enters with marginally more confidence than three days ago. His livery still doesn't fit. His hair still stands up on one side.</p>

<div class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">BRIN</span>"Morning, Your Highness. Marta sent the fresh loaves today   she said you'd want them. Also cheese pastries. She's been baking since midnight and I think the kitchen staff are staging an intervention."</div>

<p>He sets the tray down. The cheese pastries are there   golden, steaming faintly, the smell of rosemary and melted cheese cutting through every other scent in the room. Marta. Even now. Especially now.</p>

<div class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">EDRIN</span>"Brin."</div>

<div class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">BRIN</span>"Your Highness?"</div>

<p>I look at him. Sixteen. Sandy hair. Too-big livery. A boy from the tanner's family in the Lower Market who got a palace job because the crown offers patronage to common families. He's been bringing my breakfast for three weeks. He knows how I take my bread   stale, if possible. He knows I eat standing at the window. He remembers the pastry compliment and relayed it to Marta and it made her day.</p>

<p>In three days, a woman will be sitting in this room. Brin will bring her breakfast. He'll be confused. He'll adapt   servants always adapt, it's the job   but the prince he's been learning to serve will be gone, replaced by a princess he doesn't know, and the small, specific intimacy of remembering someone's breakfast preferences will have to be rebuilt from scratch.</p>

<div class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">EDRIN</span>"Thank you," I say. It comes out weighted   too much meaning for two words, too much goodbye for a boy who doesn't know it's a goodbye.</div>

<p>He blinks.</p>

<div class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">BRIN</span>"You're welcome, Your Highness. Are you... is everything alright?"</div>

<div class="dialogue"><span class="speaker">EDRIN</span>"Everything's fine. The pastries are perfect."</div>

<p>He smiles. He leaves. The door closes. The pastries are, in fact, perfect. I eat two of them standing at the window, looking down at the courtyard, and the cheese is hot and the rosemary is sharp and the last breakfast I eat as a man tastes like a childhood I didn't appreciate until it was over.</p>

<<set $d0_npc_brin to true>>
<<set $energy += 10>>
<<set $stress -= 3>>
<<set $repStaff += 1>>

<div class="scene-end">
